1
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Soul Men is a comedy, music film directed by Malcolm D. Lee.

2
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Two former backup soul singers, Louis and Floyd, have not spoken to each other in 20 years, and reluctantly agree to
travel across the country together to a reunion concert to honor their recently-deceased lead singer.

3
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Cleo, a beautiful young woman who is believed to be Floyd's
daughter, accompanies them as a new singer.

4
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Louis Hinds, played by Samuel L. Jackson.

5
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:51,000
Floyd Henderson, played by Bernie Mac.

6
00:30:54,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Cleo, played by Sharon Leal.

7
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Phillip, played by Adam Herschman.

8
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Danny Epstein, played by Sean Hayes.

9
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:27,000
Lester, played by Affion Crockett.

10
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Soul Men is a 2008 American musical comedy film directed by Malcolm D.

11
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:45,000
Lee, and starring Samuel L.

12
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:54,000
Jackson, Bernie Mac, Sharon Leal and Sean Hayes.

13
01:06:57,000 --> 01:07:03,000
The film released on November 7, 2008.

14
01:12:06,000 --> 01:12:12,000
It was one of three films featuring Mac that were released after his death (and was actually
released on the same date as another posthumous film, Madagascar: Escape 2 Africa).

15
01:17:15,000 --> 01:17:21,000
distributed by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.

16
01:22:24,000 --> 01:22:30,000
Mac and Isaac Hayes died on August 9 and 10, 2008,
respectively, and the film is dedicated to their memory.

17
01:27:33,000 --> 01:27:39,000
Director Lee said the film was heavily re-edited to soften the
tone of the film, as a tribute to the two actors.

18
01:32:42,000 --> 01:32:48,000
Critical reviews were mixed, and the film was financially unsuccessful.

19
01:37:51,000 --> 01:37:57,000
The tone is lighthearted.
